# s2_beaver_reveal_inplace (off-path)
#
# basis      s1_plaintext_free peak 3059428 kB; single pool (host). Recorder names the torch CPU
#            allocator, so ranking from the census at s1's peak (steps/s1_plaintext_free/evidence/README.md;
#            why: steps/s0_default/evidence/README.md):
#   int64 (28996,768) word-embedding shares, 4 copies   712605696 B   0.233 of the peak  <- this step
#   int64 (768,768) attention weight shares, 49         231211008 B   0.076
#   int64 (3072,768) FFN weight shares, 12              226492416 B   0.074
#   int64 (768,3072) FFN weight shares, 12              226492416 B   0.074
#   int64 (1,128,28996) one-hot temporaries, 6          178151424 B   0.058
#   plaintext float32 tracing leftovers, 196 tensors    143130624 B   0.047
#
# fix        two of four (28996,768) copies are throwaway: _arithmetic_function clones y before torch.sub
#            (arithmetic.py:359,380); all_reduce clones every input (distributed_communicator.py:195).
#            Both Beaver reveal operands have no other referrer: built without clone, reduced in place.
# free       no recomputation, no extra round, same bytes on the wire.
# draws      generate_additive_triple called with the same sizes in the same order; same arithmetic.
#            Binding here: fixed-point truncation is share-dependent (unseeded baseline: 3.8x spread).
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: libc10.so+0x4a675
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu
